  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1617.06 Inspection for Entry of Theft",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-01-10",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1617.06 Inspection for Entry of Theft. All magazines containing explosive material shall be opened and inspected at intervals of not greater than 3 days to determine whether there has been an unauthorized entry or attempted entry into the magazine, or to determine whether there has been unauthorized removal of the contents of the magazines.\n\nSource. #2220, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2837, eff 8-27-84; ss by #4584, eff 3-3-89; ss by #5996, INTERIM, eff 3-3-95, EXPIRES, 7-1-95; ss by #6054, eff 7-1-95, EXPIRED: 7-1-03\n\nNew. #8116, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04, EXPIRES: 1-10-05; ss by #8231, eff 12-20-04; ss by #10396, eff 8-15-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1600.html"
